00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.302 align:start size:84% position:16%
- There is a mental
health crisis

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:04.004 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the left is
only escalating it.

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.240 align:start size:88% position:13%
They are increasing this
mental health crisis

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.575
rather than addressing it.

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:10.710 align:start size:84% position:16%
Gender dysphoria
used to be something

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.645
that you went and got help for.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:17.550
And now it's encouraged and
it's pushed on our youth.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.887 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know what, what an
adult chooses to do, do it.

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:23.423 align:start size:88% position:13%
But when you are
confusing our children,

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.325 align:start size:88% position:13%
when you are sexualizing
our children,

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:28.294 align:start size:84% position:16%
that is where the
line has to be drawn.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.897
(upbeat music)

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:38.271
- I'm Dave Rubin, we
are in Washington DC,

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:41.174
and joining me today
is a US congresswoman

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.443 align:start size:88% position:13%
representing Colorado's
3rd district,

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.145
Congresswoman Lauren Boebert.

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:46.780
Welcome back to
the Rubin Report.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.148
- Dave, it is so
great to be back

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.916
in the Rubin Report with you.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.151
- We were supposed
to do this yesterday,

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.319 align:start size:84% position:16%
but apparently even
a congresswoman

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:57.791
doesn't have the power to stop
our endless aviation problems

00:00:57.791 --> 00:00:59.159
that we are having in
America these days.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:00.427
- Oh, no.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:01.361
You know, Republicans
are in the majority,

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:02.495
so we have a little more power,

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:05.398 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I'm not as powerful
as Tony Gonzales

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.935 align:start size:88% position:13%
who can shut down entire
border security bills

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.137 align:start size:84% position:16%
just with the
power of his words.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:14.541 align:start size:84% position:16%
No, I was stuck in
airports all day long.

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.843
I mean, if you're just
gonna count Eastern Time,

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:20.613
8:00 AM to midnight, and I
had two of my boys with me,

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.215
which some people would think

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.684
that that causes for more
stress, more of a headache,

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:25.952
but it was awesome.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.754
I had my 15 year old
and my 10 year old,

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:30.156
and we walked the
airports together,

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.825
we snuggled on airplanes,

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.993
we went and ate good
food in the airport.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.096 align:start size:88% position:13%
They wanted McDonald's,
I vetoed that

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.731 align:start size:97% position:3%
and said, "Listen, you get
McDonald's any time you want."

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.134
But it was really great just
spending the day with them

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.602
and a unique experience.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.403
Got home.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:48.007
We got home at 12:30.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.609
I put my 10 year
old in the shower.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.145
I said, "I have been with
you all day, you smell.

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.647
I made you shower before
we got on the airplane,

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.516
and I don't think
you used soap."

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.051
(Congresswoman Lauren laughing)

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:01.221
So we still didn't get to
bed till after 1:00 AM.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.589
- Do you ever wanna do that

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:03.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
with some of the
Democrats you're debating?

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:04.891
(Congresswoman Lauren laughing)

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:05.859 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Yes.
- You smell.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:06.793
I'm putting you in the shower.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:07.660
- I don't think you used soap.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.862 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Yeah.
(both laughing)

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.196 align:start size:84% position:16%
- The mom instincts
come out in me.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.364
(Congresswoman Lauren laughing)

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.565 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You know, individual
responsibilities

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:14.934 align:start size:97% position:3%
is usually not their thing.
- Right.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.270
- Do your kids and and
family come to DC often

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.439
or is this just like you
doing your thing here,

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:20.940
in and out, kind of thing?

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.109
- Yeah, so I'm pretty much
on my own for the most part.

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.712 align:start size:84% position:16%
But when their
schedule allows it,

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.080
they certainly come up here.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.481
We've pulled them out of school

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.150
to have weeks up here before,

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.185
because I had been
traveling so much

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:33.720
and just missed the
heck out of them

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.221
and said, why don't
you come out here?

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they act like they own
DC when they come here.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:40.260 align:start size:97% position:3%
They go throughout the
Capitol, the office buildings.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.128 align:start size:84% position:16%
They know which
members of Congress

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:43.596
have dogs in their office.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start position:0%
And you know, they go and storm
their offices and hang out.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.371
But this is spring break,
so I have two boys with me.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:55.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
My oldest son is
expecting his son any day.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.042 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Oh, right, right.
- So, yeah.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.477
So he couldn't come to DC...

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:59.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
- The fact that you're...
- I know. (laughs)

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.647 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Wait, how old are you?
- I'm 36.

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:02.215
- You're gonna be a
36 year old grandma.

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.516
- Yes, yes.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:05.385 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm a Gigi, Dave, I'm a Gigi.
(both laughing)

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:06.853
- How does that feel?

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.855
- You know, I'm really excited.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:11.691
So my mom, she was
18 when she had me.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:14.360 align:start size:88% position:13%
I was 18 when I had
Tyler, and now he's 18.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.029
And one of his first
comments to me was,

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.997 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Mom, it's hereditary."
- Yeah.

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.799
- I said, "Nice try.

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:21.301
It doesn't work that way."

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:24.037
But I'm really proud of him

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:26.706
and my grandson's mom
for being responsible

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.709
because they could have
taken a different route.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.811
And both of them chose life.

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:35.548
And so it wasn't anything I
had to browbeat them with.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:39.552 align:start position:0%
I very calmly had the
conversation when we found out.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.721
Just let me know if you
think something else.

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.389
I just wanna have
a talk with you

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.058
if you decide to go a
different direction.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:48.161
And both of them
were very excited

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:49.362
and wanted to move forward

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.264 align:start size:84% position:16%
and welcome this
life into the world.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.665
- Was there any part of that

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:54.167 align:start size:84% position:16%
that challenged
any of your beliefs

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.369
before you did that
sit down with them

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.804
and just realizing, you know?

00:03:57.804 --> 00:04:00.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, so I mean,
obviously I'm a Christian

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:03.209
and you know, there
are standards that
we like to uphold,

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:05.511
but none of us do it perfectly.

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:08.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the biggest
things that I look to is,

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:10.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Him who knows to do right
and doesn't, it's sin.'

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I mean, there's things
all throughout the week

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:14.120
that I know is right to do,

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.789
and sometimes I don't do them.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:19.425
And so we can nitpick

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.728
what the Bible says
is right and wrong,

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:26.032 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I think just having
that heart posture

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:28.368
of wanting to serve God
and do the right thing

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.036
is so important.

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:33.306
And I mean, would I have
chose a different path?

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:34.807
Of course.

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:38.378
But, this is where we're at
and we're all embracing it

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:40.179
and we're so happy.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:41.447
- Wait, what do you mean

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:42.415
you would've chose
a different path?

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.916 align:start size:88% position:13%
- For Tyler, for my son.
- Oh.

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.251
- Yes, yes.

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:47.120 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I mean...
- Meaning at this age?

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.055
- At this age, exactly, yeah.

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:51.924 align:start size:81% position:19%
He wanted to go
to UTI in Florida.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:54.093 align:start size:97% position:3%
He was going to graduate and
go to college in Florida.

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:58.364 align:start size:97% position:3%
And now, he's looking at
petroleum engineering classes,

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:00.566 align:start size:81% position:19%
courses at our
community college.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.002 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's a great community
college in Rifle,

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:05.038
but I get to have him
home with me longer,

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:07.507
and I get to be Gigi.

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:09.242
So certainly there
are some beliefs

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:11.144
that you're like, wait,

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.712
this isn't exactly right

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:14.514
and exactly what
we have taught you,

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:15.715
but this is where we're at

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:17.984 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we're going to teach
you about redemption

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:19.786
and how to move forward.

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:22.255
So I'm happy that
he's close to me

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:23.990
and I get to instruct him now

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.359
on how to be a loving father

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:28.027
and how to raise a baby.

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.863
- Let's do a couple things
about Colorado specifically,

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:33.066 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then we'll get to
the rest of the country.

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:37.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I did my book tour
back in May, I did Denver,

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.604
I'd stop in Denver,

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:41.407 align:start position:0%
and I was shocked at the amount
of homeless people there.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.209
Like you expect it in Seattle,

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:46.646 align:start size:97% position:3%
you expect it in San Francisco
and Portland, et cetera.

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:49.148
But I was shocked by what
was going on in Denver,

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:50.416
which is such a gorgeous city.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:51.818
And the people are
great and all that.

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:54.220
So what is going on in Denver?

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.588
- Democrats.

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:57.623
So, I mean, really
that's what happened.

00:05:57.623 --> 00:06:01.027
We had universal mail-in ballots

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:02.895
about 10 years ago go through,

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:06.632
and Democrats started taking
over every single election.

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:11.537
And unfortunately, it was when
we had our gubernatorial race

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:13.539 align:start size:84% position:16%
that elected
Governor Jared Polis.

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:17.677 align:start size:97% position:3%
And after that is when we
just saw this dramatic decline

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:18.911
in Colorado.

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:22.615
Our policies infringing
on Coloradan's rights

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.686
and then just the crime
increase, marijuana.

00:06:26.686 --> 00:06:29.389 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's legal in
Colorado, obviously.

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:31.858
And I think that that did
bring in a different...

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:33.292
- So you connect that directly

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:36.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
because as a general
rule, I'm more libertarian

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:38.297 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I do believe in
legalizing this stuff,

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:39.532
and I'm not against people

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:41.033 align:start size:84% position:16%
doing what they want
with their lives,

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:43.469
but even seeing in New York
what's going on right now,

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:45.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
the whole city just smells
like weed, basically.

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:46.806
- Yes, yes.

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:49.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't go outside in
Denver and not smell weed.

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:51.711 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it's pretty much
throughout most of the state,

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:54.147
especially in those urban areas.

00:06:54.147 --> 00:06:57.116
But I think it just
brought with it,

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.818
that legalization
brought with it

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:03.156 align:start size:84% position:16%
a different population
and certainly a
transient population.

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:06.392
And the homelessness has
just skyrocketed in Denver.

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:10.897 align:start position:0%
When we were having all the
COVID lockdowns and everything,

00:07:10.897 --> 00:07:13.800
I mean, we just had
a complete encampment

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.268 align:start size:81% position:19%
right there at the
Denver Capitol.

00:07:15.268 --> 00:07:16.536
- Yeah, I mean, you guys

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:18.137
like literal tent
cities everywhere.

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:19.071
- Yes, tent cities.
- I was shocked.

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:20.306
- Yes, and they are everywhere.

00:07:20.306 --> 00:07:22.975 align:start size:88% position:13%
And they're not doing
anything to remove them,

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:26.112 align:start position:0%
so they're enabling the problem
and it is only increasing.

00:07:26.112 --> 00:07:27.480
- What do you think of,

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.748 align:start size:84% position:16%
well, I guess I
know what you think,

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:30.450
but so Polis it seems
to me that people say,

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.919 align:start size:97% position:3%
when I'm always like, "Oh,
there's no moderate Democrat."

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:34.520 align:start size:88% position:13%
People are like, "Well,
Polis is kind of,

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.222
he's not completely insane."

00:07:36.222 --> 00:07:37.824 align:start size:84% position:16%
But it doesn't sound
like the policies

00:07:37.824 --> 00:07:39.091
are that far from
what we think...

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:41.194
- No, the policies
are very extreme.

00:07:41.194 --> 00:07:44.497
And I do like Governor Jared
Polis on a personal level.

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:46.232
I mean, we've had
some interactions

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:48.134
and he has been very kind to me,

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:51.437 align:start size:88% position:13%
but his policies do
not match that moderate

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:55.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
or libertarian mantra that
people have about him,

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:57.844 align:start size:84% position:16%
even hearing stories
of him serving

00:07:57.844 --> 00:07:59.245
in the House of Representatives

00:07:59.245 --> 00:08:01.013 align:start size:84% position:16%
is very different
than what I'm seeing

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:02.982
as him being our governor.

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:05.084 align:start size:81% position:19%
And maybe it's his
cabinet members

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:07.086 align:start size:84% position:16%
who are pushing these
extreme policies,

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:09.222 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he's kind of
going along with it.

00:08:09.222 --> 00:08:11.157
There is a super majority,

00:08:11.157 --> 00:08:13.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Democrats have a super
majority in Colorado,

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:17.530
and the state legislature
pushes extreme policies.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.932
And unfortunately those
get signed into law,

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:25.605
whether that's gun control
laws or comprehensive sex-ed

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:29.308
or vaccine mandates
for our children

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:31.511
in order to go to school.

00:08:32.645 --> 00:08:34.614 align:start size:81% position:19%
And so all of this
is so extreme,

00:08:34.614 --> 00:08:39.619 align:start size:97% position:3%
and from the top down, it
affects everyone everywhere.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:43.556 align:start size:84% position:16%
The lockdowns affected
our businesses.

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:45.591
So many were shut down, our
churches were shut down,

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:46.859
our schools were shut down.

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:51.330
People were masked up
and just lost so much.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
We didn't have a
statewide vaccine mandate

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:55.134
for the COVID vaccine.

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:57.069
And maybe that's why
people look and say,

00:08:57.069 --> 00:08:59.238
"Oh, look, he wasn't that bad."

00:08:59.238 --> 00:09:00.907
But in that circumstance,

00:09:00.907 --> 00:09:02.842
I kind of see it like
as an abused spouse,

00:09:02.842 --> 00:09:05.511
like, oh, he doesn't beat
me all the time, you know?

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:06.345 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Right, right, right.
(both laughing)

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:07.613
- We have good days.

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:08.814
