00:18:59.805 --> 00:19:01.273
It doesn't have to
be every teacher,

00:19:01.273 --> 00:19:03.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
it doesn't have to be
the majority of teachers,

00:19:03.008 --> 00:19:07.045
but even knowing that
there is someone there

00:19:07.045 --> 00:19:11.683
to stop an imminent threat,

00:19:11.683 --> 00:19:14.419 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think that is a
large enough deterrent,

00:19:14.419 --> 00:19:16.088
because even we're
hearing reports,

00:19:16.088 --> 00:19:17.556
I don't know how true they are,

00:19:17.556 --> 00:19:19.591 align:start size:97% position:3%
but we're hearing reports
that the shooter in Nashville,

00:19:19.591 --> 00:19:22.661
whom I won't name,
nor give pronouns,

00:19:24.163 --> 00:19:26.064
said this was a soft target.

00:19:26.064 --> 00:19:28.634
Like this person knew

00:19:28.634 --> 00:19:32.271
that this school was
not going to be able

00:19:32.271 --> 00:19:34.773
to stop the shooting.

00:19:34.773 --> 00:19:36.008
- So at what point though,

00:19:36.008 --> 00:19:37.209
I know you don't
wanna blame groups

00:19:37.209 --> 00:19:38.677
and I think that's important

00:19:38.677 --> 00:19:39.878
and I literally didn't
tweet about it yesterday,

00:19:39.878 --> 00:19:41.413
'cause I was just like,

00:19:41.413 --> 00:19:44.149
I just don't want to add in
the midst of the craziness.

00:19:44.149 --> 00:19:46.919
Everyone gets in on it for
clicks and all that stuff.

00:19:46.919 --> 00:19:50.088 align:start size:97% position:3%
But at what point do you
think the Democrat rhetoric,

00:19:50.088 --> 00:19:51.757
and this is what they do
to you guys all the time.

00:19:51.757 --> 00:19:53.025
The Republicans are
always defending guns

00:19:53.025 --> 00:19:54.226
and it's their fault.

00:19:54.226 --> 00:19:55.027
So I don't wanna
do that same thing.

00:19:55.027 --> 00:19:56.228
But at what point,

00:19:56.228 --> 00:19:58.497 align:start size:88% position:13%
when you constantly tell
this group of people

00:19:58.497 --> 00:19:59.831
that they're oppressed,

00:19:59.831 --> 00:20:02.701
that there's a trans genocide,

00:20:02.701 --> 00:20:05.737
all of this stuff that
is just patently untrue,

00:20:05.737 --> 00:20:08.807
at what point do you have
to look at your colleagues

00:20:08.807 --> 00:20:11.443
and be like, do you see
there is a problem here.

00:20:11.443 --> 00:20:14.279 align:start size:97% position:3%
You actually are radicalizing
a certain set of people.

00:20:14.279 --> 00:20:15.948
- No, I do think
that that's true.

00:20:15.948 --> 00:20:17.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that is something
that we need to speak of.

00:20:17.683 --> 00:20:19.218 align:start size:84% position:16%
Just this one
particular instance,

00:20:19.218 --> 00:20:21.019
I don't want to blame
all of the people,

00:20:21.019 --> 00:20:23.155
but yes, there is a
mental health crisis

00:20:23.155 --> 00:20:25.591 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the Left is
only escalating it.

00:20:25.591 --> 00:20:27.059
- Yeah.

00:20:27.059 --> 00:20:28.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
- They are increasing
this mental health crisis

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:30.028
rather than addressing it.

00:20:30.028 --> 00:20:32.164 align:start size:84% position:16%
Gender dysphoria
used to be something

00:20:32.164 --> 00:20:34.132
that you went and got help for,

00:20:34.132 --> 00:20:39.071
and now it's encouraged and
it's pushed on our youth.

00:20:39.071 --> 00:20:42.374 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know what, what an
adult chooses to do, do it.

00:20:42.374 --> 00:20:44.910 align:start size:88% position:13%
But when you are
confusing our children,

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:46.878 align:start size:88% position:13%
when you are sexualizing
our children,

00:20:46.878 --> 00:20:49.815 align:start size:84% position:16%
that is where the
line has to be drawn.

00:20:49.815 --> 00:20:52.751
When you are telling
elementary students,

00:20:52.751 --> 00:20:54.086
three-year-olds, five-year-olds,

00:20:54.086 --> 00:20:55.854
you could be a boy,
you could be a girl.

00:20:55.854 --> 00:20:57.022
Well, they could be a mermaid.

00:20:57.022 --> 00:20:58.624 align:start size:88% position:13%
I wanted to be a
mermaid when I was four.

00:20:58.624 --> 00:21:01.059 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, I lived in
the pool and you know...

00:21:01.059 --> 00:21:02.628
- Decepticon.
- Decepticon.

00:21:02.628 --> 00:21:03.862
(Congresswoman Lauren laughing)

00:21:03.862 --> 00:21:06.064
So, I mean, this is a problem.

00:21:06.064 --> 00:21:09.301
And it is radicalizing a group.

00:21:10.669 --> 00:21:13.138
I saw a CNN article that says,

00:21:13.138 --> 00:21:16.708
if you've ever tweeted
a meme of a black woman,

00:21:16.708 --> 00:21:18.844
well then that's
digital black face.

00:21:18.844 --> 00:21:21.913 align:start size:88% position:13%
This is the new,
'oppress me of the day.'

00:21:21.913 --> 00:21:23.815
You know, oppress me please.

00:21:23.815 --> 00:21:27.552 align:start position:0%
And when you're telling
someone you're not good enough,

00:21:27.552 --> 00:21:30.656
you are oppressed, you
are the lesser person,

00:21:30.656 --> 00:21:32.124
you are the lesser class,

00:21:32.124 --> 00:21:35.060
well then that's going
to get inside of them

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:39.698
and cause depression and
more mental health crises.

00:21:40.832 --> 00:21:42.901 align:start size:81% position:19%
So it is something
that I believe

00:21:42.901 --> 00:21:45.737 align:start size:97% position:3%
that the left is
radicalizing and encouraging.

00:21:45.737 --> 00:21:47.839 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So what do you do to reach
across the aisle on this?

00:21:47.839 --> 00:21:49.641 align:start size:84% position:16%
'Cause I'm doing about
10 or 12 interviews

00:21:49.641 --> 00:21:51.109 align:start size:84% position:16%
all with Republicans
when I'm here.

00:21:51.109 --> 00:21:53.879 align:start size:97% position:3%
We reached out to Democrats,
not one responded,

00:21:53.879 --> 00:21:55.847
and I spoke to Senator
Ron Johnson yesterday.

00:21:55.847 --> 00:21:57.249
He basically said,

00:21:57.249 --> 00:21:58.283 align:start size:97% position:3%
"Well, none of the
Democrats will talk to me."

00:21:58.283 --> 00:21:59.618
I spoke to Crenshaw and he said,

00:21:59.618 --> 00:22:01.653 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Well, kind of on the
DL they'll talk to him."

00:22:01.653 --> 00:22:03.722
And some of them
aren't that crazy.

00:22:03.722 --> 00:22:06.391 align:start size:88% position:13%
Gates gave me a similar
version to that.

00:22:06.391 --> 00:22:08.226
Who are the not crazy ones?

00:22:08.226 --> 00:22:09.695
Do they talk to you

00:22:09.695 --> 00:22:11.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
and is there anything that
can be done with them?

00:22:11.229 --> 00:22:13.799
I mean, if I'm too scary
of an interview for them,

00:22:13.799 --> 00:22:16.168
it's like I'm not known for
the hard wall interview.

00:22:16.168 --> 00:22:17.502
I try to listen to people.

00:22:17.502 --> 00:22:19.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yes, you do.
- But they won't sit here.

00:22:19.971 --> 00:22:21.406
That's the thing.

00:22:21.406 --> 00:22:22.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yes, well, I mean,
that's the problem because

00:22:22.674 --> 00:22:24.743
the Democrat party has
their marching orders.

00:22:24.743 --> 00:22:26.411
We saw it during
the speakers race.

00:22:26.411 --> 00:22:28.580
Everyone's yelling at
the Republicans saying,

00:22:28.580 --> 00:22:30.315
"You have to get unified.

00:22:30.315 --> 00:22:31.717
This looks crazy."

00:22:31.717 --> 00:22:33.218 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, we have
independent thought.

00:22:33.218 --> 00:22:34.786 align:start size:81% position:19%
The Democrats were
told what to do

00:22:34.786 --> 00:22:36.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they did exactly what
they were told to do.

00:22:36.655 --> 00:22:38.190
- Right, even the
radicals, like AOC.

00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:40.359
- Even the radicals, absolutely.

00:22:40.359 --> 00:22:43.395
And even the Congress
before that they had,

00:22:43.395 --> 00:22:46.331
they were forming a coup
to take down Nancy Pelosi

00:22:46.331 --> 00:22:48.033
and they took the deal.

00:22:48.033 --> 00:22:49.368
They say, "You know what,

00:22:49.368 --> 00:22:50.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
my committee
assignment's good enough.

00:22:50.469 --> 00:22:51.370
Thank you ma'am,"

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:52.504
and walked on.

00:22:56.041 --> 00:22:58.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so much of this, they
don't want to engage.

00:22:58.210 --> 00:22:59.978
We see it in debate.

00:22:59.978 --> 00:23:02.481 align:start size:84% position:16%
They want to say
their side and leave.

00:23:02.481 --> 00:23:04.182
They don't wanna hear
the opposing views.

00:23:04.182 --> 00:23:07.119 align:start size:97% position:3%
A lot of times if I'm
debating on the house floor,

00:23:07.119 --> 00:23:08.320
I'll go early.

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:09.621 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'll hear what the
Democrats have to say,

00:23:09.621 --> 00:23:12.224
my colleagues have to
say, I'll stay later.

00:23:12.224 --> 00:23:14.126
Sometimes I even ask
somebody for their time

00:23:14.126 --> 00:23:15.961
so I could go up and respond.

00:23:15.961 --> 00:23:17.162
- Does anyone else do that?

00:23:17.162 --> 00:23:18.363
I feel like nobody
listens to the talks.

00:23:18.363 --> 00:23:19.731
Like someone gets up there talk

00:23:19.731 --> 00:23:20.999
and they're like,
nobody's there,

00:23:20.999 --> 00:23:22.801 align:start size:84% position:16%
but it's on CSPAN
or we see the clips.

00:23:22.801 --> 00:23:24.102
- It is very rare,

00:23:24.102 --> 00:23:25.604
because you do have
your scheduled times

00:23:25.604 --> 00:23:26.872
and our days are
really busy here,

00:23:26.872 --> 00:23:28.607
so I understand it.

00:23:28.607 --> 00:23:31.376
But usually you go in
for your two minutes,

00:23:31.376 --> 00:23:32.711
that's what you have to speak.

00:23:32.711 --> 00:23:34.913
Maybe it's five minutes
and then you get out

00:23:34.913 --> 00:23:36.314
and you're onto
the next meeting.

00:23:36.314 --> 00:23:39.151
And it's almost feels
like it's by design

00:23:39.151 --> 00:23:42.754
to keep us so busy
that we can't engage

00:23:42.754 --> 00:23:43.688
with our colleagues.

00:23:43.688 --> 00:23:44.856
And back to the speakers race,

00:23:44.856 --> 00:23:47.192 align:start size:88% position:13%
that was one of my
favorite parts about it.

00:23:47.192 --> 00:23:51.396
Those four days, we were all
together on the house floor

00:23:51.396 --> 00:23:54.633
debating, engaging
in conversations
with our colleagues.

00:23:54.633 --> 00:23:57.636
I talked to Republicans I
had never spoke to before.

00:23:57.636 --> 00:24:00.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
I talked to Democrats I
had never spoke to before.

00:24:00.071 --> 00:24:01.773
And it was a wonderful four days

00:24:01.773 --> 00:24:04.810
of actually getting to know
and understand one another.

00:24:04.810 --> 00:24:06.745
- Were you worried that, I mean,

00:24:08.079 --> 00:24:09.714
ultimately you guys
got some concessions,

00:24:09.714 --> 00:24:12.484
but were you worried as one
of the most outspoken people

00:24:12.484 --> 00:24:13.552
sort of against McCarthy,

00:24:13.552 --> 00:24:15.086
that you were gonna pay a price,

00:24:15.086 --> 00:24:16.588 align:start size:81% position:19%
just personally
even if you got...

00:24:16.588 --> 00:24:17.856
- Oh, absolutely.

00:24:17.856 --> 00:24:21.293
But that wasn't going
to be what determined

00:24:21.293 --> 00:24:22.494
what I was doing.

00:24:22.494 --> 00:24:23.929
I couldn't say,

00:24:23.929 --> 00:24:25.797
"Oh, I'm never going to
be re-elected again."

00:24:25.797 --> 00:24:29.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
If that's my only thought
is my next election,

00:24:29.167 --> 00:24:30.836 align:start size:84% position:16%
then I have no
business being here.

00:24:30.836 --> 00:24:33.138
I need to do what
I believe is right.

00:24:33.138 --> 00:24:34.573
That's what I was
sent here to do.

00:24:34.573 --> 00:24:37.275
I convinced and promised, what,

00:24:37.275 --> 00:24:39.444
hundreds of thousands of
people that I'm a leader,

00:24:39.444 --> 00:24:41.646 align:start position:0%
that I'm strong, I'm principled.
I'm going to stand for them

00:24:41.646 --> 00:24:43.148
and fight for them.

00:24:43.148 --> 00:24:45.250
And so I wasn't going to sit
back and go along to get along

00:24:45.250 --> 00:24:46.818 align:start size:84% position:16%
and say, "Oh, my
committee assignment,

00:24:46.818 --> 00:24:49.120
oh, I don't want a primary,

00:24:49.120 --> 00:24:50.322
I don't want leadership

00:24:50.322 --> 00:24:52.324 align:start size:84% position:16%
spending money
against me in a race,"

00:24:52.324 --> 00:24:55.694
or any kind of repercussions,
whatever you could think of.

00:24:55.694 --> 00:24:57.529
I knew to do what was right.

00:24:58.697 --> 00:25:00.932 align:start size:84% position:16%
And this was all about
these negotiations

00:25:00.932 --> 00:25:03.902
that we had started in the
summer and in good faith.

00:25:03.902 --> 00:25:06.605
And I'm glad that Speaker
McCarthy saw the merit

00:25:06.605 --> 00:25:09.541
in what we were asking
for and gave them to us.

00:25:11.009 --> 00:25:13.712
I want to use more of the
tools that we've received,

00:25:13.712 --> 00:25:15.647 align:start size:97% position:3%
and some of them, it's
just not time for them yet,

00:25:15.647 --> 00:25:16.882
like the Holman rule,

00:25:16.882 --> 00:25:18.950
that'll come up more
in appropriations.

00:25:18.950 --> 00:25:22.187
But I don't want to only
admire what we received.

00:25:22.187 --> 00:25:23.822
I wanna put these tools to work.

00:25:23.822 --> 00:25:25.590 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I'm interviewing him
later today at the Capitol.

00:25:25.590 --> 00:25:28.193
Is there anything I can
push him on for you?

00:25:28.193 --> 00:25:29.394
Anything you need
a little nudge on?

00:25:29.394 --> 00:25:30.328
- I actually think...

00:25:30.328 --> 00:25:31.796
- 'Cause I like the fact that

00:25:31.796 --> 00:25:34.466
he seems like he's coming
alive with this stuff.

00:25:34.466 --> 00:25:35.700 align:start size:84% position:16%
- He does.
- It really does seem

00:25:35.700 --> 00:25:37.235 align:start size:84% position:16%
like it's happening.
- He really does.

00:25:37.235 --> 00:25:38.169
I think Speaker McCarthy's
doing a really great job,

00:25:38.169 --> 00:25:39.838
and I'm not just saying that.

00:25:39.838 --> 00:25:42.140
He is very aggressive on this.

00:25:42.140 --> 00:25:44.342 align:start size:88% position:13%
Even the January 6th
videos that he released,

00:25:44.342 --> 00:25:45.844
that wasn't part
of the concessions,

00:25:45.844 --> 00:25:47.279
that was a bonus.

00:25:47.279 --> 00:25:48.980
You know, and so
this is amazing.

00:25:48.980 --> 00:25:51.383
If there's anything that I
wanna be more aggressive on,

00:25:51.383 --> 00:25:52.450
it's subpoenas.

00:25:54.252 --> 00:25:57.923
And this isn't anything
against Chairman Comer

00:25:57.923 --> 00:25:59.424
or Pat Fallon who's
a subcommittee chair,

00:25:59.424 --> 00:26:01.593
and the subcommittee,
we had the ATF hearing.

00:26:01.593 --> 00:26:04.296 align:start size:84% position:16%
We had an ATF hearing
without the ATF.

00:26:04.296 --> 00:26:06.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want the ATF in and
they are coming in April,

00:26:06.831 --> 00:26:10.068 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I want to start
issuing these subpoenas

00:26:10.068 --> 00:26:11.636 align:start size:84% position:16%
and being very
aggressive with it.

00:26:11.636 --> 00:26:13.038
The Democrats are.

00:26:13.038 --> 00:26:14.272 align:start size:81% position:19%
- So, I'm glad
you mentioned that

00:26:14.272 --> 00:26:16.908
because you were part
of the Twitter hearings

00:26:16.908 --> 00:26:19.044 align:start size:81% position:19%
and there was a
great viral moment

00:26:19.044 --> 00:26:20.078
where you basically were like,

00:26:20.078 --> 00:26:21.379
"You guys did this to me.

00:26:21.379 --> 00:26:22.581
Like you did it to me

00:26:22.581 --> 00:26:24.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm a congresswoman."
- Yes.

00:26:24.282 --> 00:26:26.084
- And this is what I've asked
everyone else who has sat here

00:26:26.084 --> 00:26:27.352
over the last couple days,

00:26:27.352 --> 00:26:30.255
what actually comes of
this stuff other than,

00:26:30.255 --> 00:26:31.623
okay, we can expose some of it.

00:26:31.623 --> 00:26:33.525
So you bring out a
Twitter executive.

00:26:33.525 --> 00:26:35.360
He kind of did some bad stuff,

00:26:35.360 --> 00:26:37.729
sorta sometimes did
some decent stuff.

00:26:37.729 --> 00:26:39.497 align:start size:84% position:16%
But what about the
government side of it?

00:26:39.497 --> 00:26:41.399
Like when are we gonna drag

00:26:41.399 --> 00:26:44.402 align:start size:97% position:3%
or when are you guys gonna
drag out the government agents

00:26:44.402 --> 00:26:46.938 align:start size:88% position:13%
who actually were
communicating with them

00:26:46.938 --> 00:26:48.607
as opposed to the
Twitter guys who,

00:26:48.607 --> 00:26:49.841
it's not that I have
sympathy for them,

00:26:49.841 --> 00:26:51.376
but they're private employees

00:26:51.376 --> 00:26:53.912
who were probably in over
their head and whatever?

00:26:53.912 --> 00:26:58.550
- Yes, and so we did have
former FBI Agent Baker

00:26:58.550 --> 00:26:59.818
that was in there.

00:26:59.818 --> 00:27:01.052 align:start size:84% position:16%
- But he had been
appointed from Twitter

00:27:01.052 --> 00:27:02.253
- But he was working
for Twitter, correct.

00:27:02.253 --> 00:27:03.855
We do need to bring
in these people.

00:27:03.855 --> 00:27:05.523
But we called those hearings,

00:27:05.523 --> 00:27:07.626
Twitter file hearings part one.

00:27:07.626 --> 00:27:09.694
So we are going to have more.

00:27:09.694 --> 00:27:11.029
But unfortunately, Dave,

00:27:11.029 --> 00:27:13.164 align:start size:84% position:16%
I do think that
these next two years

00:27:13.164 --> 00:27:15.200
are two years of exposure.

00:27:15.200 --> 00:27:18.670
And I want to expose
the federal employees

00:27:18.670 --> 00:27:20.705 align:start size:88% position:13%
who are involved in
this more than anything.

00:27:20.705 --> 00:27:24.275 align:start position:0%
And then hopefully, the
Inspectors Generals look at this

00:27:24.275 --> 00:27:27.078
and there's some
sort of referral

00:27:27.078 --> 00:27:30.215
that we can actually
get criminal referrals

00:27:30.215 --> 00:27:32.550
for some of the things
that have been done.

00:27:32.550 --> 00:27:35.687
But I don't know if we can do
that in this administration.

00:27:35.687 --> 00:27:37.856
- So basically you need a
Republican administration

00:27:37.856 --> 00:27:39.290
to actually do anything.

00:27:39.290 --> 00:27:41.626 align:start position:0%
So the hope is you can get
people to know enough about it.

00:27:41.626 --> 00:27:42.861 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Right.
- Temporarily.

00:27:42.861 --> 00:27:45.797
- All the top guys are
Biden's guys right now.

00:27:45.797 --> 00:27:48.133
So that is our biggest struggle.

00:27:48.133 --> 00:27:49.701
So we have to build this case.

00:27:49.701 --> 00:27:52.003
We have to expose
what's been hidden

00:27:52.003 --> 00:27:54.339
from the American
people for years.

00:27:54.339 --> 00:27:57.175
There has been no oversight in
the House of Representatives

00:27:57.175 --> 00:28:00.145
and there still isn't much
oversight in the Senate.

00:28:00.145 --> 00:28:01.813
The Democrats have
the gavel there,

00:28:01.813 --> 00:28:04.349
and they aren't going to
bring in serious people

00:28:04.349 --> 00:28:05.617
to have this oversight.

00:28:05.617 --> 00:28:07.752
So it's our job to carry
the weight of the House

00:28:07.752 --> 00:28:10.121 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the Senate and
make up for those years

00:28:10.121 --> 00:28:12.223
where there was no
oversight conducted.

00:28:12.223 --> 00:28:13.625
- Not to beat a dead horse,

00:28:13.625 --> 00:28:15.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
but were there any
Democrats in that hearing

00:28:15.860 --> 00:28:17.562
that were like, oh, actually,

00:28:17.562 --> 00:28:18.997
even though I'm a Democrat

00:28:18.997 --> 00:28:20.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were mostly
going after Conservatives,

00:28:20.665 --> 00:28:22.667
this is a violation of
the First Amendment.

00:28:22.667 --> 00:28:25.603
Maybe even on the DL, did
anyone say anything to you?

00:28:25.603 --> 00:28:29.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
- You know, if there
were, I didn't hear of it.

00:28:29.007 --> 00:28:32.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so everything was
extreme, MAGA Republicans.

00:28:32.577 --> 00:28:34.713
And you know, I did set the
record straight and said,

00:28:34.713 --> 00:28:37.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Listen, we are not
extreme MAGA Republicans,

00:28:37.615 --> 00:28:41.019 align:start size:81% position:19%
it is ultra MAGA."
(both laughing)

00:28:41.019 --> 00:28:45.423
But we were exposing how
the federal government

00:28:45.423 --> 00:28:46.791
worked with Twitter

00:28:46.791 --> 00:28:48.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
to suppress the
Hunter-Biden laptop story.

00:28:48.927 --> 00:28:50.662
They didn't wanna touch that.

00:28:50.662 --> 00:28:52.197
Everything is January 6th.

00:28:52.197 --> 00:28:54.899 align:start size:84% position:16%
And they're using
what they know works

00:28:54.899 --> 00:28:57.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it did work for
them in the last election.

00:28:57.936 --> 00:29:01.606
But now we're exposing what
happened during January 6th,

00:29:01.606 --> 00:29:03.007 align:start size:81% position:19%
what happened with
the censorship,

00:29:03.007 --> 00:29:04.476 align:start size:81% position:19%
what happened with
the lockdowns,

00:29:04.476 --> 00:29:06.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
the fraud, the waste abuse
with the COVID funds.

00:29:06.811 --> 00:29:08.680
And Afghanistan,

00:29:08.680 --> 00:29:11.082 align:start size:88% position:13%
other committees are
having hearings on that.

00:29:12.550 --> 00:29:17.188
We had a soldier that had the
suicide bomber in his sights,

00:29:18.857 --> 00:29:21.659
and he was not allowed to
neutralize that threat,

00:29:21.659 --> 00:29:22.894
in his sights.

00:29:22.894 --> 00:29:26.464
And now we have 13 of
our soldiers killed.

00:29:26.464 --> 00:29:28.233
I mean, absolutely disgusting,

00:29:28.233 --> 00:29:30.368
but we are exposing
what was going on,

00:29:30.368 --> 00:29:32.070 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the American people
are gonna see it.

00:29:32.070 --> 00:29:35.640 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I hope in the
next two to four years

00:29:35.640 --> 00:29:37.308
we have actual accountability.

00:29:37.308 --> 00:29:40.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want any show pony
hearings like Benghazi.

00:29:40.645 --> 00:29:42.680
I want people to be
held accountable,

00:29:42.680 --> 00:29:44.182
and so do the American people.

00:29:44.182 --> 00:29:47.051
- Do you think, it's kind of
funny when Biden keeps saying,

00:29:47.051 --> 00:29:49.788
the extreme MAGA Republicans
or ultra MAGA or whatever,

00:29:49.788 --> 00:29:52.190 align:start size:97% position:3%
like he's sort of talking
about your wing of the thing

00:29:52.190 --> 00:29:54.692 align:start size:97% position:3%
as if you guys are
completely running the show.

00:29:54.692 --> 00:29:57.629
And the whole point is that
you guys were on the outside

00:29:57.629 --> 00:29:59.030
and had to fight
for a lot of that.

00:29:59.030 --> 00:30:01.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he's basically
trying to paint everybody

00:30:01.166 --> 00:30:04.202
as if you and Matt and Gates
and a couple other people...

00:30:04.202 --> 00:30:05.136
- Well, we will take it.

00:30:05.136 --> 00:30:06.604
If they want us to run the show,

00:30:06.604 --> 00:30:08.573 align:start size:97% position:3%
let's run it because we have
some really great ideas.

00:30:08.573 --> 00:30:11.976
I mean, look at even the
debt ceiling proposal.

00:30:11.976 --> 00:30:13.211
It was a House Freedom Caucus

00:30:13.211 --> 00:30:15.513 align:start size:84% position:16%
that came out and
said, we have a plan.

00:30:15.513 --> 00:30:17.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
We aren't going to default
on our nation's debt,

00:30:17.949 --> 00:30:19.484 align:start size:88% position:13%
but we're gonna claw
back some of this stuff.

00:30:19.484 --> 00:30:21.186 align:start size:84% position:16%
Some of the unspent
COVID funding,

00:30:22.620 --> 00:30:25.623
the student loan program,
we're taking that back.

00:30:25.623 --> 00:30:27.759
I mean, if you wanna just
do pennies on the dollar,

00:30:27.759 --> 00:30:32.197
we're not building your
$500 million FBI building

00:30:33.565 --> 00:30:35.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you need, that
you're brand new building.

00:30:35.233 --> 00:30:36.701
And so there's a...

00:30:36.701 --> 00:30:37.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Is that one of the
things they're going for,

00:30:37.969 --> 00:30:40.238 align:start size:84% position:16%
the FBI needs a $500
million building?

00:30:40.238 --> 00:30:41.206
- Yeah.

00:30:41.206 --> 00:30:42.841
You know, really important.

00:30:42.841 --> 00:30:44.042
Gosh.

00:30:44.042 --> 00:30:45.376 align:start size:84% position:16%
So there are things
that we can...

00:30:45.376 --> 00:30:46.511
- They really deserve it

00:30:46.511 --> 00:30:47.478
after the last couple of years

00:30:47.478 --> 00:30:48.546
- They've worked so hard.

00:30:48.546 --> 00:30:50.481
(Congresswoman Lauren laughing)

00:30:50.481 --> 00:30:52.417
It was really the
raid, they're like,

00:30:52.417 --> 00:30:55.954 align:start size:97% position:3%
"Hey, we need a bonus after
this Mar-a-Lago raid."

00:30:55.954 --> 00:30:58.022
So, we have a plan,

00:30:58.022 --> 00:31:02.927 align:start size:97% position:3%
Joe Biden's plan it
increases taxes on everyone.

00:31:04.095 --> 00:31:06.464
They are doing nothing
to reduce inflation,

00:31:06.464 --> 00:31:09.167
to increase energy development.

00:31:09.167 --> 00:31:11.569 align:start size:97% position:3%
Everything that they're
doing will increase inflation

00:31:11.569 --> 00:31:12.737
and reduce energy.

00:31:12.737 --> 00:31:14.005
We have 20 million Americans

00:31:14.005 --> 00:31:17.108
that can't afford their
utility bills right now.

00:31:17.108 --> 00:31:18.743
We have a wide open
southern border.

00:31:18.743 --> 00:31:20.078
We want it secure.

00:31:20.078 --> 00:31:23.114
We want the flow of
fentanyl to stop.

00:31:23.114 --> 00:31:24.949
And so we have a plan,

00:31:24.949 --> 00:31:28.353
and I told Joe Biden in our
press conference, I said,

00:31:28.353 --> 00:31:29.787 align:start size:84% position:16%
"We're meeting
tonight on the Hill.

00:31:29.787 --> 00:31:31.856 align:start size:97% position:3%
You wanna come here, put
down your ice cream, join us.

00:31:31.856 --> 00:31:33.358
We'll have a conversation."

00:31:33.358 --> 00:31:34.192
And...

00:31:34.192 --> 00:31:35.693
- You know, it's funny.

00:31:35.693 --> 00:31:37.629
The guy keeps coming
downstairs and says,

00:31:37.629 --> 00:31:39.163 align:start size:88% position:13%
the only reason I'm
down here for ice cream.

00:31:39.163 --> 00:31:40.632
And I'm starting to believe it.

00:31:40.632 --> 00:31:42.333 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like, that's the only reason
he's coming downstairs.

00:31:42.333 --> 00:31:43.868
Like, I like ice cream.

00:31:43.868 --> 00:31:45.136
And everybody's like,

00:31:45.136 --> 00:31:46.271 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Oh, there's the old man
who likes ice cream."

00:31:46.271 --> 00:31:47.739
- Exactly.

00:31:47.739 --> 00:31:50.074 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, we hear about the
horrible tragedy in Nashville

00:31:50.074 --> 00:31:52.310 align:start size:97% position:3%
and he says, "I hear there's
chocolate chip cookies."

00:31:52.310 --> 00:31:54.412
- He literally did like a
five minute standup routine

00:31:54.412 --> 00:31:55.747 align:start size:81% position:19%
about ice cream
when he came down.

00:31:55.747 --> 00:31:57.015 align:start size:72% position:28%
I mean, nuts.
- Yes.

00:31:57.015 --> 00:31:58.283
- All right, let me
ask you one more,

00:31:58.283 --> 00:31:59.918
I know you hit the gym
before you got here.

00:31:59.918 --> 00:32:00.852 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, I did.
- You got a long day of stuff.

00:32:00.852 --> 00:32:01.653
You gotta get outta here.

00:32:01.653 --> 00:32:02.787
One more for you.

00:32:02.787 --> 00:32:04.322
(Congresswoman Lauren laughing)

00:32:04.322 --> 00:32:05.690
So you talked about what's
gonna happen in two years,

00:32:05.690 --> 00:32:07.191
hopefully.

00:32:07.191 --> 00:32:10.228
Obviously, this thing seems to
be like going back and forth

00:32:10.228 --> 00:32:11.562 align:start size:81% position:19%
between the Trump,
DeSantis thing.

00:32:11.562 --> 00:32:13.164
I know you love Trump.

00:32:13.164 --> 00:32:15.867
You obviously said some nice
things about DeSantis here.

00:32:15.867 --> 00:32:17.936
I think you have a sense of
where I'm at on this thing.

00:32:17.936 --> 00:32:20.471
What's your general take?

00:32:20.471 --> 00:32:21.773
And actually, do you
think there is a way

00:32:21.773 --> 00:32:23.174
which would be my preference,

00:32:23.174 --> 00:32:25.476
that it doesn't have to
end up in destruction

00:32:25.476 --> 00:32:27.045
of one or both?

00:32:27.045 --> 00:32:28.680
That would be the best way,

00:32:28.680 --> 00:32:29.514 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I just don't know
if it's possible.

00:32:29.514 --> 00:32:30.348
- Correct.

00:32:31.749 --> 00:32:32.984
At this point, I don't know
if it's possible either.

00:32:32.984 --> 00:32:34.485
I think there's
room in this tent

00:32:34.485 --> 00:32:37.889
for both President Trump
and Governor Ron DeSantis.

00:32:39.691 --> 00:32:41.793 align:start size:84% position:16%
I would love for
this to not end ugly.

00:32:41.793 --> 00:32:43.594
I have endorsed President Trump.

00:32:43.594 --> 00:32:45.029
I do endorse President Trump.

00:32:45.029 --> 00:32:47.598 align:start size:84% position:16%
I believe that he
will be our nominee.

00:32:47.598 --> 00:32:49.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, Governor
DeSantis has not announced

00:32:49.834 --> 00:32:51.369
